Package: MBbioeq
Title: Model-Based Bioequivalence Analysis Using SAEM and TOST
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Eden", "BETE", email = "eden.bete.etu@univ-lille.fr", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Celia", "BENGUENNA", email = "celia.benguenna.etu@univ-lille.fr", role = c("aut")))
Description: Performs model-based bioequivalence analysis for parallel-arm studies
    using Stochastic Approximation Expectation-Maximization (SAEM) estimation
    (via the 'saemix' package). Supports one-compartment pharmacokinetic models
    with or without absorption lag time. Implements the Two One-Sided Tests
    (TOST) with asymptotic normal and Gallant small-sample corrections, and the
    Bayesian-Optimal Test (BOT) based on the folded-normal distribution.
    Delta-method variance propagation is used for the Cmax endpoint. Flexible
    random-effects structures (diagonal, full, block) and multiple residual
    error models (additive, proportional, combined) are supported. Includes
    diagnostic plots: spaghetti plots of individual profiles, forest plots of
    geometric mean ratios with 90 percent confidence intervals, and folded-normal
    decision plots for BOT.
